LINE 48 
LINE 49 Note: Overloaded with a version with a signature matching the equivalent function on the CTF. This ensures that the exchange can be used with this contract without modification.
LINE 50 
LINE 51 ## `safeTransferFrom`
LINE 52 
LINE 53 Provided to ensure compatibility with contracts that expect to be able to transfer tokens from this contract, e.g., the NegRisk CTFExchange.
LINE 54 
LINE 55 In order to transfer tokens this way, the owner must approve this contract _and_ the calling contract.
LINE 56 
LINE 57 ## `redeemPositions`
LINE 58 
LINE 59 Redeems a pair of YES and NO tokens for their underlying collateral, once the question is resolved.
LINE 60 
LINE 61 Unwraps the resulting wrapped collateral into the original collateral before returning to the user.
LINE 62 
LINE 63 ### Parameters
LINE 64 
LINE 65 ```[solidity]
LINE 66 address _conditionId,
LINE 67 uint256[] _amounts
LINE 68 ```
MATCH_END
MATCH_BEGIN docs__NegRiskAdapter.md LINES 74 99
LINE 74 The user must hold at least `_amount` of each NO token.
LINE 75 
LINE 76 If the market has `n` questions, and the user converts `_amount` of `m` NO tokens, the user receive `_amount * (m-1)` collateral and `_amount` each of the complimentary YES tokens.
LINE 77 
LINE 78 Supposing that exactly one questions resolves true, these two positions have equivalent final values. In the event that all questions resolve false, the resulting position is worth _less_ than the original position. It is not possible for more than one question to resolve true.
LINE 79 
LINE 80 There is an optional `feeRate` market parameter which exists to implement a fee on the conversion. Collected fees are sent to the `vault` address.
LINE 81 
LINE 82 It is necessary to synthetically mint wrapped collateral in order to collateralize the resulting YES tokens. Careful book keeping ensures that the value of outstanding YES tokens will never exceed the value of collateral in the wrapped collateral contract. In this process, it is necessary to burn NO tokens; they are sent to an uncontrolled burn address.
LINE 83 
LINE 84 ### Parameters
LINE 85 
LINE 86 ```[solidity]
LINE 87 bytes32 _marketId
LINE 88 uint256 _indexSet
LINE 89 uint256 _amount
LINE 90 ```
LINE 91 
